# Proposed features recognized from outer_profile.step by sidecar/import_step.py
# (contract v1 -- see sidecar/CONTRACT.md). Review before use:
# recognition proposes, it does not machine.

# F1: cylindrical, axis +Z, full revolution, material inside (a standing boss), flat top cap F3, the base at z=13.0 is the head's own underside, and nothing from above reaches what is under the head -- F2 (the head's underside), F4 (a wall of the neck) -- so the boss is proposed down to z=10.0, the floor F5 it stands over, and the program leaves the material under the head standing (CHECKLIST row 2.4)
# finish the wall with: run Side(tool=..., surface=F1_Boss, stepover=...)  [stepover is the ring spacing up the wall]
# the tool rides outside at R + r_tool (convex flank; finish_cylinder's mirror)
# the walls end at z=13.0 on the head's own underside; the neck, the pad and the pad's
# foot bevels under it are out of reach from above, so the boss runs down to z=10.0, the
# floor it stands over, and the program leaves what is under the head standing
feature F1_Boss CylinderBoss(dia=14.0, extent=6.0, x=42.0, y=36.0, z=10.0)

# F3: planar, normal +Z, topmost planar face (CHECKLIST row 1.1)
feature F3_Top Plane(z=16.0)

